{{- /*
  beads-issues/push-and-open-pr — headless (no mitto_ui_* calls) push +
  PR-create-or-update, safe to call exactly once from an automated loop
  driver's Done branch.

  Called EXACTLY ONCE, inline in each driver's Done branch (e.g.
  loop-fixing-bug Step 3d, loop-implementing-feature Step 3e, mention-driver
  Step 3f) — never per phase. A feature bead crosses four phases in four
  separate turns; opening a PR per phase would spam four PRs for one bead.

  Composes git/shared/identify-remote-branch (resolves <target-remote> /
  <target-branch> / <push-remote>) and git/shared/behind-base-count
  (detection only — no interactive verdict fragment is pulled in, so nothing
  here prompts the user).

  Unlike git/shared/create-or-update-pr (built around mitto_ui_form +
  mitto_ui_textbox for title/description/reviewers), this fragment is
  headless-only by construction: it always uses `gh pr create --fill` /
  `glab mr create --fill` and reports the URL back onto the bead as a
  comment instead of presenting a form.

  Callers pass a dict:
    "Ctx"    — the full render context (`.`), forwarded verbatim to the
               nested identify-remote-branch / behind-base-count calls.
    "Target" — the resolved bead ID. Required; the PR URL is commented here.

  Preconditions: the working tree is clean (everything already committed)
  and the caller is already on the bead's feature branch (usually via
  beads-issues/shared/ensure-bead-branch).
*/ -}}
{{- $ctx := .Ctx -}}
{{- $target := .Target -}}
{{ template "git/shared/identify-remote-branch" $ctx }}

#### Preflight: not behind the base

{{ template "git/shared/behind-base-count" $ctx }}

If behind (`> 0`), do **not** push: `bd comment {{ $target }}` explaining the
branch is `<N>` commits behind `<target-remote>/<target-branch>` and needs a
rebase first, then stop — do not open or update a PR against a stale base.

#### Push and create-or-update the PR

Idempotent — check for an existing PR before creating a new one:

```bash
existing_url=$(gh pr view <branch-name> --json url,state -q '.url' 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$existing_url" ]; then
  git push <push-remote> <branch-name>
  pr_url="$existing_url"
else
  git push -u <push-remote> <branch-name>
  gh pr create --fill --base <target-branch>          # GitHub
  # glab mr create --fill                              # GitLab
  pr_url=$(gh pr view <branch-name> --json url -q '.url')
fi
```

#### Report back

```bash
bd comment {{ $target }} "PR: $pr_url"
```

No `mitto_ui_*` calls anywhere in this fragment — safe for unattended runs.
